.TH KISSLOCK "1" "November 2026" "kisslock" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
kisslock \- an ultra-simple screen locker for Wayland

.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fIkisslock\fR [OPTIONS...]
.PP
Locks your Wayland session.
.PP

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " CONFIG"
Read configuration from
.I CONFIG
instead of the default configuration file.
.TP
.B -h
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
.B -v
Display the version and exit.

.SH CONFIGURATION
.B kisslock
reads its configuration from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kisslock/config .
If
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset or empty, it uses
.IR ~/.config/kisslock/config .
The configuration file is optional. If it does not exist, built-in defaults are used.

Each setting consists of a key followed by a value, separated by whitespace. Blank lines and lines beginning with
.B #
are ignored. Unknown keys and invalid values produce a warning and are ignored.

.TP
.B idle
The background color displayed while the locker is idle.

.TP
.B input
The background color displayed while input is being entered.

.TP
.B fail
The background color displayed after an unsuccessful authentication attempt.

.RS
Colors must be specified as six hexadecimal digits in
.I RRGGBB
format. A leading
.B #
or
.B 0x
is also accepted.
.RE

.TP
.B fail_ms
The duration, in milliseconds, for which the failure color is displayed after an unsuccessful authentication attempt. Valid values are between 1 and 60000.

.TP
.B clock
Whether to display the clock at the top of the lock screen. Accepted values are
.BR on ,
.BR yes ,
.BR 1 ,
.BR off ,
.BR no ,
and
.BR 0 .

.TP
.B hours
The clock's hour format. Accepted values are
.BR 12 ,
.BR ampm ,
or
.BR 12h
for 12-hour time, and
.BR 24
or
.B 24h
for 24-hour time.

.SS Defaults
If a setting is omitted, its built-in default is used:

.nf
idle     000000
input    005577
fail     CC3333
fail_ms  1000
clock    on
hours    24
.fi

.SS Example
.nf
# Colors are RRGGBB. A leading # or 0x is accepted.
idle 000000
input 005577
fail CC3333

# How long the fail color stays up, in milliseconds.
fail_ms 1000

# Display the clock.
clock on

# Use 24-hour time.
hours 24
.fi

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Specifies the base directory for user-specific configuration files. If unset or empty,
.B kisslock
uses
.IR ~/.config
instead.

